  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only PCA with multiprofile avgpool is the best configuration so far (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), while image-only models are much weaker and transformer aggregation is worse than avgpool for PCA. The key remaining uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation can improve on PCA under this best profile/aggregation setting. config_005 changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile and avgpool, isolating the representation effect. It is the best next experiment because RNA is currently the dominant modality, so this has high expected leverage and creates a stronger baseline before testing multimodal fusion."
